/**
 * TASK: Make a text field refuse anything that is not a digit.
 *
 * A KEY_TYPED event can be CANCELLED: calling e.consume() inside keyTyped
 * stops the character ever reaching the text field. Register a KeyListener
 * on the field named "amount" whose keyTyped applies these rules:
 *
 *   - a digit ('0'..'9') is allowed, UNLESS the field already holds 4
 *     characters, in which case it is consumed too
 *   - backspace (the char '\b') is ALWAYS allowed, even when the field is
 *     full, otherwise the user could never correct a mistake
 *   - anything else -- letters, spaces, '.', '-' -- is consumed
 *
 * Every consumed character also adds 1 to rejectedCount().
 *
 * Example: with the field holding "12", typing '7' is allowed; typing 'x'
 * is consumed and rejectedCount() becomes 1.
 *
 * Use Character.isDigit(char) for the digit test.
 *
 * No window is ever opened -- the tests build KeyEvents by hand, hand them
 * straight to the registered listener and then ask event.isConsumed().
 */
